:9230,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":41,"p":null,"l":"","x":"ZXh0PjwvZz48ZyB0cmFuc2Zvcm09J3RyYW5zbGF0ZSgwKSc+PHRleHQgeT0nNic+MzE8L3RleHQ+PC9nPjwvZz48ZyB0cmFuc2Zvcm09J3RyYW5zbGF0ZSgxMSwxNSknPjxnIHRyYW5zZm9ybT0ndHJhbnNsYXRlKDYyNiknPjx0ZXh0IHk9JzYnPjx0c3Bhbj5vcGNv"},{"r":9231,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":42,"p":null,"l":"","x":"bj5mdW5jdDM8L3RzcGFuPjwvdGV4dD48L2c+PGcgdHJhbnNmb3JtPSd0cmFuc2xhdGUoMzEzKSc+PHRleHQgeT0nNic+PHRzcGFuPnJzMTwvdHNwYW4+PC90ZXh0PjwvZz48ZyB0cmFuc2Zvcm09J3RyYW5zbGF0ZSgxMjMpJz48dGV4dCB5PSc2Jz48dHNwYW4+aW1t"},{"r":9232,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":43,"p":null,"l":"","x":"alt=\"Diagram\" width=\"800\" height=\"56\">"},{"r":9233,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":44,"p":null,"l":"","x":"RV32I Arithmetic Instructions:"},{"r":9234,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":45,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| Instruction         | Effect                                           | Description            |\n|:--------------------|:-------------------------------------------------|:-----------------------|\n"},{"r":9235,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":46,"p":null,"l":"","x":"Addition and subtraction do not check for overflow and underflow.\n\nRV32I Control Instructions:\n\n| Instruction         | Efect                                        |                       |\n|:-------"},{"r":9236,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":47,"p":null,"l":"","x":"To allow flexible use of registers, the P0 compiler maintains a set `regs` of registers in use. For RISC-V, `GPregs` are the general-purpose registers:\n```python\nGPregs = {'s2','s3','s4','s5','s6','s7"},{"r":9237,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":48,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| E           | code(E)                                 | register | condition               |\n|:------------|:----------------------------------------|:---------|:------------------------|\n| `x`  | `"},{"r":9238,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":49,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| `+ E`       | `code(E)`   |  |\n| `– E`       | `code(E)`<br>`sub reg, zero, reg` | `reg` | `reg` is the register of `E`   |\n| $$E_1 + E_2$$   | `code(E₁)`<br>`code(E₂)`<br>`add reg, reg₁, reg₂` | `r"},{"r":9239,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":50,"p":null,"l":"","x":"For boolean expression, the translation scheme is analogous, except that no code is generated for the negation of a relational operation, only the relation is negated:"},{"r":9240,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":51,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| E           | code(E)                                 | register | condition               |\n|:------------|:----------------------------------|:------|:------------------------|\n| `false`    | `add"},{"r":9241,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":52,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| $E_1 < E_2$<br>$$not(E_1 \\ge E_2)$$  | `code(E₁)`<br>`code(E₂)`<br>`slt reg, reg₁, reg₂`| `reg` | `reg₁` is the register of $$E_1$$ <br> `reg₂` is the register of $$E_2$$ <br> `reg` is a fresh regis"},{"r":9242,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":53,"p":null,"l":"","x":"### Translation Scheme for Statements and Declarations\n\nThe translation scheme for P0 statements is:"},{"r":9243,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":54,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| S           | code(S)                                 | condition             |\n|:------------|:----------------------------------------|:------------------------|\n| `x := E`  | `code(E)`<br>`sw reg"},{"r":9244,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":55,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| $$S_1; …; S_n$$    | `code(S₁)` <br> `…` <br> `code(Sₙ)`                                  |                        |\n| `if E then S` | `code(E)`<br>`beq reg, zero, L1`<br>`L2:`<br>  ` code(S)`<br>`L"},{"r":9245,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":56,"p":null,"l":"","x":"The translation scheme for declarations is:\n\n| D                 | code(D)                             | effect                       |\n|:------------------|:------------------------------------|:----"},{"r":9246,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":57,"p":null,"l":"","x":"The translation scheme for a program is:\n\n| P                 | code(P)                             |  comment                  |\n|:------------------|:------------------------------------|:----------"},{"r":9247,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":58,"p":null,"l":"","x":"### Translation Scheme for Boolean Operators\n\nIn P0 boolean operators `and` and `or` evaluate conditionally:\n```pascal\np and q = if p then q else false\np or q = if p then true else q\n```\n\nThe followin"},{"r":9248,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":59,"p":null,"l":"","x":"The P0 compiler implements an improved scheme that does not store intermediate results but branches to the locations where execution is to be continued right away.\n\n### Translation Scheme for Arrays\n\n"},{"r":9249,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":60,"p":null,"l":"","x":"Local arrays are dynamically allocated in memory in a stack.\n\nWith $$A = [l .. u] \\to T$$, the translation scheme for programs with local array declarations is:\n\n| D          | code(D)          |    c"},{"r":9250,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":61,"p":null,"l":"","x":"For example:\n\n<code style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\nvar i, j: integer\nvar x: [1..5] → integer\nprogram p\n    i := x[j + 3]\n</code>\n\n<pre style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\n    .data\ni_:\t.space 4\nj"},{"r":9251,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":62,"p":null,"l":"","x":"<code style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\nvar i, j: integer\nprogram p\n  var x: [1..5] → integer\n    i := x[j + 3]\n</code>\n\n<pre style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\n\t.data\ni_:\t.space 4\nj_:\t.space 4\n\t.t"},{"r":9252,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":63,"p":null,"l":"","x":"| S           | code(S)                                 | comment |\n|:------------|:----------------------------------------|:--------|\n| `x[E] := F` | `code(E)`<br>`addi reg₁, reg₁, -x.lower`<br>`add"},{"r":9253,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":64,"p":null,"l":"","x":"For example:\n\n<code style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\nvar i, j: integer\nvar x: [1..5] → integer\nprogram p\n    x[i + 3] := 7\n</code>\n\n<pre style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\n\t.data\ni_:\t.space 4\nj_:\t"},{"r":9254,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":65,"p":null,"l":"","x":"<code style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\nvar i, j: integer\nprogram p\n  var x: [1..5] → integer\n    x[i + 3] := 7\n</code>\n\n<pre style=\"float:left;margin-left:2em\">\n\t.data\ni_:\t.space 4\nj_:\t.space 4\n\t.t"},{"r":9255,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":66,"p":null,"l":"","x":"Pseudoinstruction            | Base Instruction(s)                                           | Meaning   | Comment\n:----------------------------|:------------------------------------------------------"},{"r":9256,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":67,"p":null,"l":"","x":"fs{w\\|d} rd, symbol, rt      | auipc rt, symbol[31:12]; fs{w\\|d} rd, symbol[11:0]\\(rt\\)      | Floating-point store global\nnop                          | addi x0, x0, 0                                "},{"r":9257,"d":2607,"s":"note","t":"8 A RISC Architecture as Target","c":68,"p":null,"l":"","x":"seqz rd, rs                  | sltiu rd, rs, 1                                               | Set if = zero\nsnez rd, rs                  | sltu rd, x0, rs            